  "major": "sociology-cultural-anthropology-bs-9db661c0",
  "major_name": "Sociology and Cultural Anthropology",
  "degree": "BS",
  "campus": "Boston",
  "college": "College of Social Sciences and Humanities",
  "overview_text": "The Department of Sociology and Anthropology at Northeastern University offers a combined major in sociology and cultural anthropology. Students learn the disciplinary histories, practices, and methods of sociology and sociocultural anthropology, identify foundational and contemporary debates within and across these two disciplines, and evaluate their contributions to our understanding of local and global societies and cultures. The combined major offers students various opportunities for community engagement, experiential learning, and for gaining research skills using quantitative and qualitative methods.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nSociology Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nSociology Core Courses\nSOCL 1101\nIntroduction to Sociology\n4\nSOCL 3300\nSocial Theory\n4\nor\nANTH 3421\nFoundations of Anthropological Theory\nMethodological Requirements\nSOCL 2320\nStatistical Analysis in Sociology\n4\nor\nINSH 3102\nIntroduction to Statistics in the Social Sciences\nSOCL 2321\nResearch Methods in Sociology\n4\nor\nINSH 3101\nResearch Methods in the Social Sciences\nAdditional Required Methodological Training\nComplete one of the following:\n4\nCS 2000\nand\nCS 2001\nIntroduction to Program Design and Implementation\nand Lab for CS 2000\nCOMM 2105\nSocial Networks\nDS 3000\nFoundations of Data Science\nINSH 2102\nBostonography: The City through Data, Texts, Maps, and Networks\nSOCL 2323\nEthnographic Methods\nSOCL 3487\nApplied Sociology: Practice and Theory\nSociology Electives\nIntroductory electives\nComplete two courses from the following range not used to fulfill another requirement:\n8\nSOCL 1101\nto SOCL 2999\nIntermediate Electives\nComplete two courses from the following range not used to fulfill another requirement:\n8\nSOCL 3000 to SOCL 4999\nCultural Anthropology Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nCultural Anthropology Core Courses\nANTH 1101\nPeoples and Cultures\n4\nANTH 3410\nEthnographic Field Experience\n4\nAnthropology Electives\nComplete five ANTH electives between\nANTH 1101\nand ANTH 4999 not used to fulfill other requirements. One study-abroad course may count toward this requirement with prior permission from the department.\n20\nAdvanced Area Courses\nComplete two area courses between ANTH 4101 and\nANTH 4520\nnot used to fulfill another requirement.  Area courses taken in addition to these two classes may count as electives.\n8\nIntegrative Requirement and Capstone\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nIntegrative Requirement\nANTH 2305\nGlobal Markets and Local Culture\n4\nCapstone\nChoose one of the following:\n4\nANTH 4600\nSenior Seminar\nANTH 4100\nMaking Anthropology Public\nSOCL 4600\nSenior Seminar\nSociology and Cultural Anthropology Major Grade Requirement\nA GPA of 2.000 across all major courses is required.\nSociology and Cultural Anthropology Combined Major Credit Requirement\nComplete 80 semester hours in the major.\nExperiential Liberal Arts\nAll students in this College of Social Sciences and Humanities program are required to complete the\nExperiential Liberal Arts Requirement\n.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
